  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Suppose $n$ is a positive odd integer. Show that\n$$x^n+y^n=(x+y)(x^{n-1}-x^{n-2}y+\\cdots-xy^{n-2}+y^{n-1}).$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Expanding the right-hand side cancels every mixed term, leaving $x^n+y^n$.",
      "worked": "For $n=1$, the second factor is $1$, so the identity holds. For odd $n\\ge3$, expand the right-hand side:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x+y)(x^{n-1}-x^{n-2}y+\\cdots-xy^{n-2}+y^{n-1})&=x^n-x^{n-1}y+\\cdots-x^2y^{n-2}+xy^{n-1}\\\\&\\qquad+yx^{n-1}-x^{n-2}y^2+\\cdots-xy^{n-1}+y^n\\\\&=x^n+y^n.\\end{align*}$$\nThe mixed terms cancel in pairs. Since $n$ is odd, the final term is $+y^n$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
  },
